# `make runlist-gate` runs with this directory as its working directory, so every
# artifact aircc and KernelCache produce lands here rather than in a build tree.
# Eleven of them were committed by mistake in bf69ed69 -- the nine .o files were
# the only tracked object files in the repository, and air.mlir/air.elf are
# aircc intermediates that nothing reads and that are rewritten on every run.
*.o
air.mlir
air.elf
air.insts.bin
air.xclbin
# The shared-xclbin chain writes one intermediate per link (`air_shared_0`..N):
# each aircc invocation needs its OWN output name, because feeding a compile the
# file it is about to write makes xclbinutil refuse. Only the last link holds
# every kernel, and KernelCache copies that one into the mode's cache.
air_shared_*.xclbin
air_shared_*.insts.bin
air_project/

# opcheck.py writes its machine-readable verdicts here on every run. They are
# measurements, not sources: the gate regenerates them, and the durable record
# of what was measured lives in kernel_registry/. results/fault/ holds the
# negative-control runs, kept in a subdirectory so an injected run can never be
# mistaken for -- or overwrite -- a clean one.
results/

# The registry sweep's per-candidate scratch: aircc builds each candidate in its
# own directory under here and the directory is removed as soon as the verdict is
# checkpointed, so anything left is the debris of a killed run. sweep/results/ is
# already covered by the results/ rule above -- those are the checkpoints, and
# the durable record of what they decided is the kernel_registry rows.
sweep/work/
